t the desired version from the navigation pane on the left.</p> <div class=\"section\" id=\"section6345152111712\"><a name=\"section6345152111712\"></a><a name=\"section6345152111712\"></a><h4>DevEco Studio 26.0.0 Release (26.0.0.821)</h4></div> <div class=\"section\" id=\"section1121115514191\"><a name=\"section1121115514191\"></a><a name=\"section1121115514191\"></a><h4>[h2]Compatibility</h4><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p152111571911\">The following table lists the tools provided by DevEco Studio 26.0.0.821, along with their corresponding development-state version and supported API versions.</p>  <div class=\"tablenoborder\"><table id=\"table9211175181911\"><caption><b>Table 1 </b>DevEco Studio</caption><thead><tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row12119515193\"><th align=\"left\" class=\"cellrowborder\" id=\"mcps1.3.3.3.2.4.1.1\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p421118511199\">Item</p> </th> <th align=\"left\" class=\"cellrowborder\" id=\"mcps1.3.3.3.2.4.1.2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p7212859195\">Version</p> </th> <th align=\"left\" class=\"cellrowborder\" id=\"mcps1.3.3.3.2.4.1.3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p162124515191\">Description</p> </th> </tr> </thead> <tbody><tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row721215519196\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p112121254197\">HarmonyOS SDK</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1921215101910\">HarmonyOS 26.0.0 Release SDK</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p112121352196\">-</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row42121158195\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p121205111919\">HarmonyOS Emulator</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1421275151919\">26.0.0.400</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p521295121911\">Emulator.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row1521211517198\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p112126515196\">Hvigor</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p3213125171917\">6.26.4</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p19213359191\">Compilation and build tool for projects with API version 10 or later.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row92131250194\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p5213195191910\">ohpm</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p3213205131915\">26.0.0.630</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p2213852198\">Package management tool for OpenHarmony third-party libraries.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row142139511914\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p13213352197\">Node.js</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p621345141912\">24.14.1</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1321355141911\">Runtime environment for tools such as Hvigor and ohpm.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row112135541919\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p121417512194\">modelVersion</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1821417517193\">26.0.0</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p22144519194\">Version number in the development state.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row1021410551912\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p221420520198\"><a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-profile-app#section45865492619\" target=\"_blank\">compatibleSdkVersion</a></p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p9214165141915\">Earliest compatible version: 4.0.0(10)</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1621418591913\">Earliest version compatible with the application/atomic service.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row1021413515198\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1221415516196\"><a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-profile-app#section45865492619\" target=\"_blank\">compileSdkVersion</a></p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p172151451193\">26.0.0</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1821565101919\">SDK version for building the application/atomic service.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row12215350193\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p112155571912\"><a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-profile-app#section45865492619\" target=\"_blank\">targetSdkVersion</a></p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1215185121914\">4.0.0(10)–26.0.0</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.33333333333333%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p52153511910\">Target SDK version of the application/atomic service, which is between <strong>compatibleSdkVersion</strong> and <strong>compileSdkVersion</strong>.</p> </td> </tr>  </tbody></table> </div> <p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p13215452194\">The following table lists the command line tools that work with DevEco Studio 26.0.0.821, along with their corresponding development-state version and supported API versions.</p>  <div class=\"tablenoborder\"><table id=\"table15215135131913\"><caption><b>Table 2 </b>Command line tools</caption><thead><tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row14216195171917\"><th align=\"left\" class=\"cellrowborder\" id=\"mcps1.3.3.5.2.4.1.1\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1721613531920\">Item</p> </th> <th align=\"left\" class=\"cellrowborder\" id=\"mcps1.3.3.5.2.4.1.2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p821619518195\">Version</p> </th> <th align=\"left\" class=\"cellrowborder\" id=\"mcps1.3.3.5.2.4.1.3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p13216135191913\">Description</p> </th> </tr> </thead> <tbody><tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row621665191915\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1821665151913\">Command Line</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p421616511912\">26.0.0.821</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p122167581917\">Command line tool set.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row8216185111917\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p2021675201912\">codelinter</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p15217195101913\">6.0.240</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p221755121918\">Tool for checking and repairing code.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row92177591919\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p4217956195\">hstack</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p32179512193\">6.1.0</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p3217253198\">Tool for restoring the source code stack from the crash stack of an obfuscated release application.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row621713561916\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p821719541913\">hvigorw</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p221715171920\">6.26.4</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p82171571915\">Compilation and build tool for projects with API version 10 or later.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row221745111917\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p3217195141914\">ohpm</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1321813520195\">26.0.0.630</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1821855171920\">Package management tool for OpenHarmony third-party libraries.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row32183591910\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1121811516196\">HarmonyOS Emulator</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1321811514195\">26.0.0.400</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p721813511915\">Emulator.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row15218195101915\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1521810512190\">Node.js</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p19218195171913\">24.14.1</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p12218145101918\">Runtime environment for tools such as codelinter, hvigorw, hstack, and ohpm.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row2218105121910\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p021845191910\">sdk</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p12183516194\">HarmonyOS 26.0.0 Release SDK</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1121820516192\">-</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row4219152194\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1121919512191\">modelVersion</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p122191657194\">26.0.0</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p19219459199\">Version number in the development state.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row1321975131915\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p32191151198\"><a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-profile-app#section45865492619\" target=\"_blank\">compatibleSdkVersion</a></p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p2219105161915\">Earliest compatible version: 4.0.0(10)</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p112199591914\">Earliest version compatible with the application/atomic service.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row1321917518192\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p52191057190\"><a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-profile-app#section45865492619\" target=\"_blank\">compileSdkVersion</a></p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p8219135131910\">26.0.0</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1021945171910\">SDK version for building the application/atomic service.</p> </td> </tr> <tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row1219165161919\"><td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.339999999999996%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p19220953193\"><a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-profile-app#section45865492619\" target=\"_blank\">targetSdkVersion</a></p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.300000000000004%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1022010521911\">4.0.0(10)–26.0.0</p> </td> <td class=\"cellrowborder\" valign=\"top\" width=\"33.36%\"><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p112206591919\">Target SDK version of the application/atomic service, which is between <strong>compatibleSdkVersion</strong> and <strong>compileSdkVersion</strong>.</p> </td> </tr>  </tbody></table> </div> </div> <div class=\"section\" id=\"section1420262341910\"><a name=\"section1420262341910\"></a><a name=\"section1420262341910\"></a><h4>[h2]New and Enhanced Features</h4><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p42026235194\"><strong>Environment setup</strong></p> <ul id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__ul82031423181911\"><li id=\"li9286204318611\">Adds support for displaying, by default, the highest API version whose cumulative device share exceeds 90% as the Compatible SDK when creating a project. Adds the View API version distribution button for viewing the usage share of each API version across HarmonyOS devices. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-create-new-project\" target=\"_blank\">Creating a Project</a>.</li></ul> <p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p17203122312197\"><strong>Writing and debugging apps</strong></p> <ul id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__ul159442022133814\"><li id=\"li1150234515508\">Adds support for viewing more state variable binding relationships in ArkUI components. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-editer-overview#section2541105019101\" target=\"_blank\">Editor Basics</a>.</li><li id=\"li835116654819\">Optimizes symbol import handling when files are moved across modules. The index is updated accordingly when files are moved into or out of a module. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-code-refactoring#section634374493316\" target=\"_blank\">Code Refactoring</a>.</li><li id=\"li142015581707\">Adds support for external USB cameras in the Emulator. When no camera is available, the Emulator provides a virtual camera for simulating the photo capture process. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-emulator-more-features#section11725194916439\" target=\"_blank\">Camera</a>.</li><li id=\"li3968162142715\">Adds support for simulating network disconnection in the Emulator. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-emulator-access-network#section115741355151910\" target=\"_blank\">Network Disconnection Simulation</a>.</li><li id=\"li14924104294017\">Adds support for using commands to obtain UI layout information, tap and swipe the screen, and enter text in the Emulator. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-emulator-command-line#section830618485420\" target=\"_blank\">Using the Emulator via the CLI</a>.</li><li id=\"li17498185115714\">Adds support for using the mouse wheel in the crown area of the wearable emulator to simulate crown rotation. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-emulator-more-features#section772115543124\" target=\"_blank\">Crown</a>.</li><li id=\"li1298016280416\">Adds location simulation capabilities to DevEco Studio for debugging and testing location-related app features. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-mock-location\" target=\"_blank\">Location Simulation</a>.</li><li id=\"li8331952144513\">Enhances database debugging with support for executing multiple SQL statements and executing one or more selected SQL statements. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-database-inspector\" target=\"_blank\">Database Debugging</a>.</li><li id=\"li1794417226386\">Adds support in DevEco Studio for parsing app coredump files to help you quickly locate issues. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-analyze-dump\" target=\"_blank\">Parsing App minidump/coredump Files</a>.</li><li id=\"li1557148185612\">Adds support in HWASan for parsing the pseudocode, method parameters, and variable names and values corresponding to an error stack. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hwasan#section1080616409587\" target=\"_blank\">Using HWASan</a>.</li><li id=\"li196241326175919\">Adds support for collecting incremental code coverage statistics in instrument, local, and black-box coverage tests. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-instrument-test#section14255191913322\" target=\"_blank\">Running Instrument Tests from the CLI</a>, <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-local-test#section1722814418378\" target=\"_blank\">Running Local Tests from the CLI</a>, and <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-ui-test#section2863134631313\" target=\"_blank\">Black-Box Coverage Testing</a>.</li><li id=\"li12204112321913\">Adds support for providing a problem description and uploading image or video files when submitting DevEco Studio logs. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-log-postback\" target=\"_blank\">Uploading Logs</a>.</li></ul> <p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p152041235198\"><strong>Building apps</strong></p> <ul id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__ul820462318198\"><li id=\"li442116003913\">Adds the <strong>deduplicateSo</strong> field under <strong>packOptions</strong> in the project-level <strong>build-profile.json5</strong> file. This field specifies whether to remove duplicate SO files from HAPs and HSPs when building an app to reduce the app bundle size. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-profile-app\" target=\"_blank\">Project-level build-profile.json5 File</a>.</li><li id=\"li253375371610\">Adds support for merging and packaging a bytecode HAR together with all its dependencies into a standalone HAR package that has no external dependencies and can be used directly. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-har#section121297571296\" target=\"_blank\">Merging Multiple HARs for Packaging</a>.</li><li id=\"li2974813171017\">Adds support for configuring dependencies by <strong>target</strong>, <strong>product</strong>, and <strong>buildMode</strong> to build artifacts for multiple targets. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-customized-multi-targets-and-products-guides#section8222113911814\" target=\"_blank\">Configuring Multi-Target Dependencies Using a Plugin</a>.</li></ul> <p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p2205923101914\"><strong>Optimizing app performance</strong></p> <ul id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__ul94517285292\"><li id=\"li645228152917\">Adds the following capabilities to the ArkTS Snapshot lane. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-snapshot-basic-operations\" target=\"_blank\">Basic Operations with Memory Snapshot Analysis</a><ul id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__ul14220312015\"><li id=\"li10402459165919\">Adds support for obtaining the dominator tree of a node with one click. By displaying the dominator chain from GC Roots to the target instance in the dominator tree, you can directly identify the dominator responsible for a memory leak. Breaking the reference from the dominator in the path releases the associated memory, enabling more precise and efficient memory leak troubleshooting.</li><li id=\"li44021759125916\">Adds support for exporting data on the <strong>Shortest Paths</strong> tab to a local directory.</li><li id=\"li840335915919\">Adds support for viewing unobfuscated source code paths for shortest paths in ArkTS heap snapshots and navigating to the corresponding code locations in the project, facilitating debugging.</li><li id=\"li04031059135919\">Adds support for displaying constructors or objects based on different clustering rules in the <strong>Statistics</strong> area of the ArkTS Snapshot lane.</li><li id=\"li15404959175917\">Adds support for locating a target object by object ID in the <strong>Statistics</strong> area of the ArkTS Snapshot lane.</li><li id=\"li1040455985915\">Adds support for importing one or more <strong>.jsleaklist</strong> files independently, with the matching <strong>.rawheap</strong> files automatically imported. When one or more <strong>.rawheap</strong> files are imported, the matching <strong>.jsleaklist</strong> files are also automatically imported.</li></ul> </li><li id=\"li220612212012\">Adds the following capabilities to the Allocation template. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-insight-session-allocations-memory\" target=\"_blank\">Memory Analysis Overview</a>.<ul id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__ul6271541114\"><li id=\"li0783152113\">Adds the <strong>Native Leaks</strong> lane for marking memory leak locations.</li><li id=\"li1783924114\">Adds support for parsing memory objects in the ArkTS Snapshot lane.</li><li id=\"li67836211115\">Adds support for exporting allocation stack data to a local directory.</li><li id=\"li10891142512465\">Adds support for displaying the call stack with the largest memory allocation that passes through a selected stack frame and the ArkTS object list in the <strong>More</strong> area. This capability is available when recording the ArkTS Snapshot lane, regardless of whether statistics mode is enabled. To use this capability, select a range in the <strong>All Heap &amp; Anonymous VM</strong>, <strong>All Heap</strong>, or <strong>Native Heap</strong> sub-lane and click any stack frame.</li><li id=\"li19989349114013\">Adds the <strong>Collect Only Unreleased Memory Events</strong> option, which controls whether call stack data for released memory is retained during recording.</li></ul> </li><li id=\"li195686256119\">Adds the <strong>FileSystem</strong> template for locating I/O latency issues by analyzing the read and write duration of logical and physical I/O for the app and the entire device (all apps on the device), together with app logic. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-profiler-filesystem\" target=\"_blank\">I/O Latency Analysis: FileSystem</a>.</li><li id=\"li15447461724\">Adds support for displaying call stacks for release apps with <strong>profileable</strong> set to <strong>true</strong> in the <strong>app.json5</strong> file. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-insight-session-time\" target=\"_blank\">Basic Time Analysis: Time</a>.</li></ul> <p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p354245144713\"><strong>Command line tools</strong></p> <ul id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__ul137341900484\"><li id=\"li117342017480\">Adds support for specifying a file for stack parsing with the hstack tool. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-command-line-hstack\" target=\"_blank\">Using hstack</a>.</li><li id=\"li36401038259\">Adds the <strong>symlink_for_local_dep</strong> option to the <strong>ohpmrc</strong> configuration file. During <strong>ohpm install</strong>, symbolic links can be created for the extracted paths of local HAR dependencies. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-ohpmrc\" target=\"_blank\">ohpmrc</a>.</li><li id=\"li029119574620\">Adds support for <strong>--no</strong> options to ohpm commands whose parameters are of the Boolean type and default to <strong>true</strong>, including <strong>--no-strict_ssl</strong>, <strong>--no-resolve_conflict</strong>, <strong>--no-install_all</strong>, and <strong>--no-experimental-concurrently-safe</strong>. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-ohpm-common-commands\" target=\"_blank\">Common Commands</a>.</li><li id=\"li1798621710499\">Adds the arktsdoc tool, which can quickly generate reference documentation from information to be exposed externally in code files, such as variables, methods, interfaces, and classes, through the command line. For details, see <a href=\"https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-command-line-arktsdoc\" target=\"_blank\">ArkTSDoc Generator (arktsdoc)</a>.</li></ul> </div> <div class=\"section\" id=\"section16422186360\"><a name=\"section16422186360\"></a><a name=\"section16422186360\"></a><h4>DevEco Studio 26.0.0 Beta2 (26.0.0.621)</h4></div> <div class=\"section\" id=\"section614710599612\"><a name=\"section614710599612\"></a><a name=\"section614710599612\"></a><h4>[h2]Compatibility</h4><p id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__p1814712591361\">The following table lists the tools provided by DevEco Studio 26.0.0.621, along with their corresponding development-state version and supported API versions.</p>  <div class=\"tablenoborder\"><table id=\"table1114720591867\"><caption><b>Table 3 </b>DevEco Studio</caption><thead><tr id=\"EN-US_TOPIC_0000002588787318__row131488598620\"><th align=\"left\" class=\"cellrowborder\" id=\"mcps1.3.6.3.2.4.1.1\"