hypium_tests/network_isolation/README.md:22:No arguments also means check. This mode only reads ABI sizes/offsets, administrator-token status, fixed file presence/hash and, if all target options are supplied, process guards. It never calls EngineOpen or any WFP API. The `nativeWfpCalls:0` field records that code path; it is not a trace of an elevated experiment. If the copied tool does not exist, basic check still succeeds and reports its absence; live target validation remains unverified.
hypium_tests/network_isolation/README.md:75:State literals are `IDLE_UNBLOCKED`, `BLOCKED`, `EXITED_UNBLOCKED`, `ERROR_UNBLOCKED`, and exceptional `ERROR_CLEANUP_UNCONFIRMED`. The last state means NativeClose or the fresh removal observer failed: never claim recovery from that snapshot; the process exits with code 4, followed by independent recovery verification. `cleanupUnconfirmed:true` and `terminationReason:cleanup_removal_unconfirmed` identify the observer failure; the retained filters are historical IDs whose absence could not be confirmed. A later no-op Close cannot erase that failure. The normal error exit code is 3. `terminationReason` is null while running and records exit_request/console_cancel or the specific failed guard/deadline/lease/API cause at termination. Deliberately stopping heartbeat should produce `controller_lease_expired`, then successful Close/removal verification, `ERROR_UNBLOCKED` and exit 3; any missing verification must fail the facility gate.
hypium_tests/network_isolation/README.md:79:After a real main-engine Close succeeds, `session_closed` records the native return separately with `removalVerified:false/verificationPending:true`. Before clearing the actual owned IDs/key, a fresh observer engine opens a `FWPM_TXN_READ_ONLY=1` transaction. `cleanup_filter_query` records each actual filter ID/key/layer, returnCode and expectedReturnCode `0x80320003` (FWP_E_FILTER_NOT_FOUND); `cleanup_sublayer_query` records the owned GUID and expected `0x80320007` (FWP_E_SUBLAYER_NOT_FOUND). Return 0 (still present), access errors, open/transaction/log failures or any other error do not prove removal. `cleanup_observer_call` logs open, readonly begin, abort and observer close; all exit paths attempt Close even if query/abort/log fails. `cleanup_verification` summarizes `success`, original `filters`, `subLayerGuid`, `readOnlyTransaction:true`, `observerClosed` and expected return codes. Only strict NOT_FOUND results plus successful observer cleanup/evidence yield success. Idle Close opens no observer. There is no external inspect mode, no guessed ID input and no Add or policy mutation in this observer; `--check` never reaches it.
hypium_tests/network_isolation/README.md:94:The removal observer additionally follows [TransactionBegin/read-only transaction](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fwpmu/nf-fwpmu-fwpmtransactionbegin0), [SubLayerGetByKey](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fwpmu/nf-fwpmu-fwpmsublayergetbykey0) and Microsoft's [WFP error codes](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fwp/wfp-error-codes). The raw WinSDK fwpmu.h defines FWPM_TXN_READ_ONLY as 0x00000001. The implementation role has not executed any observer/WFP call.
